    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Claims the evidence does not support
    </h2>

    <ul style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:22px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Instant brightening.</strong> The trials in these reviews ran for days to months, and none of the reviews describes an instant effect. Anything that looks bright in minutes is a surface effect.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Extra hydration.</strong> In the systematic review, hydration improved equally on skin treated with vitamin C and on skin treated with a placebo.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37128827/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>4</sup></a> Vitamin C is not a moisturiser, so pair it with one.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Replacing sunscreen.</strong> Vitamin C supports skin that is dealing with sun exposure,<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29104718/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>1</sup></a> but it does not block UV the way sunscreen does.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>The more, the better.</strong> A bigger number on the label does not guarantee a better result, because stability and absorption decide how much reaches the skin.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29104718/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>1</sup></a>
</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Claim by claim
    </h2>

    <div style="margin:24px 0 34px;overflow-x:auto;border-top:2px solid #181818;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.25);">
        <table style="width:100%;min-width:620px;border-collapse:collapse;text-align:left;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;">
